{
  "//": "Lineage: the registry of Craft apps. Written by hand, except each app's upstream block, which `mise run apps:fetch` rewrites from GitHub (docs_port is the port the app's own docs use in examples). Read by mise-tasks/gen, which generates mise.toml, .mcp.json and mcp-live.json from it, and by mise-tasks/status. An app with an mcp block is checked end to end; in mcp.live, {port} stands for mcp.port.",
  "apps": [
    {
      "id": "cadcraft",
      "name": "CADCraft",
      "repo": "storytold/cadcraft",
      "version": "0.13.0",
      "install": {
        "cli": "cadcraft-cli-*-macos-universal.zip",
        "cli_bin": "cadcraft-cli",
        "app": "cadcraft-*-macos-universal.dmg"
      },
      "bundle": {
        "name": "CADCraft.app",
        "executable": "CADCraft"
      },
      "mcp": {
        "port": 7979,
        "live": [
          "--connect",
          "127.0.0.1:{port}",
          "--lazy",
          "--launch"
        ],
        "opens_itself": true
      },
      "checked": {
        "version": "0.13.0",
        "on": "2026-10-26"
      },
      "limits": [
        "The first live call right after --launch opens the app can fail with 'missing or invalid control token': the bridge reads the old token before the app writes a new one (upstream #2087). The error says it is safe to send again, and the retry works."
      ],
      "upstream": {
        "about": "CADCraft: computer-aided design and drafting — an open-source, clean-room AutoCAD-style app in pure Rust",
        "latest": "0.13.0",
        "docs": "https://github.com/storytold/cadcraft/blob/main/docs/mcp.md",
        "docs_port": 7979,
        "cli_platforms": [
          "macos-universal"
        ],
        "app_platforms": [
          "freebsd-x86_64",
          "linux-aarch64",
          "linux-riscv64",
          "linux-x86_64",
          "macos-universal",
          "windows-arm64",
          "windows-x64",
          "windows-x86"
        ]
      }
    },
